menu "Lua TTS module"

config LUA_TTS_MEMORY_PROFILING
    bool "Enable Lua TTS memory profiling logs"
    default n
    help
        Enable detailed heap and current-task stack high-water logs around Lua
        TTS playback, HTTP/TLS setup, audio conversion, and cleanup checkpoints.
        Keep this disabled for normal firmware builds because it adds verbose
        diagnostic logs.

config LUA_TTS_CHUNK_MS
    int "Lua TTS source PCM chunk duration in milliseconds"
    range 10 120
    default 30
    help
        Configure how much provider PCM the Lua TTS sink accumulates before
        converting and writing to the codec. Smaller values reduce each
        synchronous codec write window and can make streamed playback more
        responsive to network bursts, at the cost of more frequent conversion
        and write calls.

config LUA_TTS_SOURCE_BUFFER_MS
    int "Lua TTS source PCM ring buffer duration in milliseconds"
    range 0 500
    default 120
    help
        Configure the source PCM stream buffer used to decouple network TTS
        delivery from codec writes. The buffer stores provider PCM before ASRC,
        so MiMo 24 kHz mono 16-bit PCM costs about 48 bytes per millisecond.
        Set to 0 to disable buffered playback and use the synchronous path.

config LUA_TTS_PREBUFFER_MS
    int "Lua TTS source PCM prebuffer duration in milliseconds"
    range 0 250
    default 60
    help
        Configure how much source PCM must be queued before the playback task
        starts writing to the codec. This absorbs short network/SSE delivery
        gaps without buffering the larger converted output PCM.

endmenu
